{"chunk_id": "9a3a4abe680e", "text": "This section recounts the violent destruction of Daksha\u2019s sacrifice after Daksha insults Shiva. From Shiva\u2019s wrath is born the terrifying warrior Virabhadra, accompanied by Bhadrakali and vast hordes of spirits. They storm the sacrificial grounds, unleashing cosmic chaos\u2014darkness spreads, mountains shake, and the sacred ritual is torn apart as the spirits devour offerings and terrify the gods. When confronted, Virabhadra declares he has come solely to destroy the sacrifice as an instrument of Shiva\u2019s anger. Terrified, Daksha finally bows to Shiva and offers an immense hymn praising him as the universal being present in all forms of existence\u2014time, nature, sacrifice, and destruction. Shiva appears from the sacrificial fire, accepts the praise, and grants Daksha a boon, restoring meaning to the ruined rite.\nVirabhadra destroys Daksha\u2019s sacrifice under Shiva\u2019s wrath, after which Daksha appeases Shiva with an immense hymn praising him as the cosmic absolute.\nThemes: divine wrath, destruction of Daksha's sacrifice, cosmic nature of Shiva, repentance and appeasement, hymnic theology", "vector": [-0.014772642403841019, -0.027454057708382607, -0.00880058016628027, 0.014692210592329502, -0.023579925298690796, 0.02642184868454933, -0.03984055668115616, -0.027118925005197525, 1.4583501979359426e-05, -0.00868663564324379, 0.007949343882501125, 0.01748051308095455, 0.010020462796092033, 0.004296399187296629, 0.0045678564347326756, 0.009839490987360477, 0.042199891060590744, -0.015295449644327164, 0.02975977025926113, 0.012835576198995113, 0.003967969212681055, -0.0006409409688785672, 0.006414436735212803, 0.01760116033256054, -0.012795360758900642, 0.015067558735609055, 0.013224329799413681, -0.020094547420740128, 0.022333232685923576, 0.008840796537697315, -0.0009433981031179428, -0.010771160013973713, -0.0041858055628836155, -0.00783539842814207, -0.022923065349459648, -0.011488343589007854, 0.000147144